# A worktree the harness creates (see .gitignore) is a full, independent
# checkout under here -- without this, prettier double-visits (and can fail
# on) that copy's own in-progress state, which is a different session's WIP.
.claude/worktrees/
# Verbatim copies of the org's guard starters (monte3l/.github, blueprint/files/).
# Reformatting one would make it a custom copy that a template sync stops
# refreshing, and a refresh that Prettier then rejects would fail the Format
# check. The push guard and its helper are one unit: refresh both together.
.claude/hooks/guard-double-background.mjs
.claude/hooks/guard-git-push-signed.mjs
.claude/hooks/guard-secret-writes.mjs
# Shipped by the harness-extras pack, not the baseline. Prettier ignores a path
# that does not exist, so this costs nothing when the pack is not installed.
.claude/hooks/guard-shell-portability.mjs
bin/lib/signed-range.mjs
# What groundwork recorded at bootstrap (a lock, pristine copies of every file it
# wrote, a pack ledger). The lock and ledger are written by the CLI and by
# /customize, and the copies must stay byte-identical to what was installed, so
# Prettier must not reformat any of it.
.groundwork/
